{"kind":"assert","text":"C2 rulings on dd21b684. The list is accepted as the authority that\nsection 9 item 3 of the state seed note asks for.\n\na. One representative test for the platform catch sites. The record\n   does not depend on the site, so one `gateRules` guard that catches\n   the throw and returns null is the witness. Keep the other three\n   tests of your item 6.\nb. The replica gives a plain `Own`. It implements neither\n   `retainedRow` nor `retainedBirth`, and C2 has no test of\n   `readRetainedUses`. No judge and no fold reads those ports.\nc. A position above the replica's head answers null. The prediction\n   is the scope's judgment at the replica's head, and the scope at\n   that head holds no such entry. The prediction states its head.\nd. The client's fault is named `UnheldEntry`. The C2 head changes the\n   name in `notes/2026-11-13-state-seed.md`, and changes nothing else\n   in that note. The review request names the change.\ne. A throw of `judgeAct` with an empty record is the judge's own\n   failure, and the client throws it on. Two limits. The throw\n   reaches the author's own call and no subscriber. It does not stop\n   the replica or the feed, because the fold did not fail.\nf. The test seam in the replica's entry store is accepted. The\n   package entry does not export it.\n\nThe replica builds its `Own` in `packages/client`. Add no export to\n`packages/derive`. Four places now build an `Own`: `ownOf` in scope,\n`floorOwn` in replay, the story in define, and the client. I put that\non the list of the consolidation review.\n\nC2 starts in source when NF-5 is in source review order: C1, NF-5,\nC2. It needs IE-1, FG-1 and PG-1 on main before its gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}